/-! # Strict tensor augmentations from Koszul powers to ideal-power quotients

Source: Stacks Project, Tags 0921, 0922 and 06YU; blueprint order 1259, steps 1--3.
(blueprint: new-s3-koszul-quotient-tensor-augmentation).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe t
open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits MonoidalCategory
namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
noncomputable section
set_option autoImplicit false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency true

/-- The quotient augmentation after tensoring one fixed complex, with its unit,
vanishing and strict transition formulas.

Source: Stacks Project, Tags 0921, 0922 and 06YU; blueprint order 1259, steps 1--3.
(blueprint: new-s3-koszul-quotient-tensor-augmentation).

Proof: take the specified coefficient augmentations and exterior transitions from
noetherian_koszul_augmentation_pro_zero, on the lifted coefficient ring. Use the canonical
quotient equivalence from the lifted-ring quotient to ULift (Λ/I^(n+1)). In degree zero
the augmentation is the exterior-degree-zero equivalence followed by the quotient map;
all positive exterior degrees map to zero. The
only differential requiring a check is the one into exterior degree zero; its image
is generated by f_j^(n+1), hence vanishes in this quotient. Reindex cohomologically,
apply the constant-module sheafification functor, and tensor with M.complex. On the
summand of bidegree (p,0), use the scalar-extension balancing map from M^p tensor
(Λ/I^(n+1))_X to the scalar restriction of its changed module, sending m tensor b to
b tensor m; on every other summand use zero. The coproduct universal property gives
the degree-p maps. The tensor differential and the preceding augmentation check show
that these maps commute with differentials. The degree-zero unit gives exactly the
local formula defining adicReductionAugmentation. Koszul power transitions act as the
identity in degree zero, and quotient transitions preserve residue classes, proving
the strict transition equations. This also covers r=0 and the zero ring. -/
theorem koszulQuotientTensorAugmentation (X : Scheme.{t}) (Λ : Type t) [CommRing Λ]
    (d : CompleteCoefficientDatum Λ) (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → Λ)
    (hf : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = d.ideal) :
    ∃ (v : ∀ (K : proEtaleDerivedCategory X Λ) (M : AdicKFlatModel X Λ K) (n : ℕ),
        @Quiver.Hom (CochainComplex
          (SheafOfModules.{t + 1} (adicModuleRing X Λ)) ℤ) inferInstance
          (koszulTensor X Λ r f M.complex n) (adicReductionComplex X d M n)),
      (∀ (K : proEtaleDerivedCategory X Λ)
        (M : AdicKFlatModel X Λ K) (n : ℕ), koszulTensorUnit X Λ r f M.complex n ≫ v K M n =
        adicReductionAugmentation X d M n) ∧
      (∀ (K : proEtaleDerivedCategory X Λ)
        (M : AdicKFlatModel X Λ K) (n : ℕ) (p q : ℤ) (hq : q ≠ 0),
        HomologicalComplex.ιMapBifunctor M.complex (koszulPowerSheaf X Λ r f n)
          (@curriedTensor _ _ (SheafOfModules.monoidalCategory (adicConstantRing X Λ)))
          (ComplexShape.up ℤ) p q (p + q) rfl ≫ (v K M n).f (p + q) = 0) ∧
      (∀ (K : proEtaleDerivedCategory X Λ)
        (M : AdicKFlatModel X Λ K) (n : ℕ), v K M (n + 1) ≫ adicReductionComplexStep X d M n =
        koszulTensorTransition X Λ r f M.complex n ≫ v K M n) := by
  sorry

end
end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
